"""Every prediction this project recorded, and whether it survived. Item I, from the source.

The paper wants to claim it separated confirmatory from exploratory work. Asserting that is
worth nothing; the evidence is that predictions were written down *before* runs and reported
whether or not they held. Since the queue runner requires a `predicted` field on every job,
the record exists as data rather than as recollection -- this reads it back.

Outcomes cannot be inferred automatically (a prediction is prose, and whether it held is a
judgement made when the result was written up), so the verdicts live in VERDICTS below,
keyed by job id, each with the result number where the call was made. A job with no verdict
prints as UNJUDGED, which is the honest state for anything not yet written up and stops this
from quietly turning into a self-congratulatory tally.
"""
